Description: Linux, Windows and macOS virtual machines on Qualcomm Gunyah
 GunyahVM runs virtual machines on Snapdragon tablets with the Gunyah
 hypervisor, shown inside the application with GPU acceleration. One package
 holds the GTK and command-line frontends, ordinary-user supervision, the
 pinned crosvm and virglrenderer runtime, the Linux guest kernel and Mesa,
 and the macOS boot kit. macOS is created from Apple's own servers on the
 device; GunyahVM ships no Apple software.
 Created and maintained by yzddMr6
